Smiling faintly, hands folded in front of her. <b>I’ve always loved working with herbs. There’s something… magical about them. The way they can heal, soothe… or harm.</b> She laughs softly, though it seems almost too delicate, too calculated.
<b>I run the apothecary, so if you ever need anything, just let me know. The people here rely on me for medicine, tonics… even poisons.</b> Her voice is casual, but there’s a flicker of something in her eyes—something darker.
<b>This town… We all have our roles. Sofia leads, Daren works the forge, Jude keeps the library. And me? I take care of people in my own way.</b> She tilts her head slightly, observing your reaction.
<b>I don’t know much about solving crimes, but… I do know people.</b> Her gaze sharpens just slightly. She hesitates, then speaks in a lower voice, as if confessing a secret.
<b>If you ask me… Ren is suspicious. He found the body, didn’t he? What if… what if he saw something he’s not telling us?</b> She frowns, pressing her lips together. <b>I don’t know, maybe I’m just grasping at straws… I just—</b> She exhales, shaking her head.
<b>I don’t have the answers you need, but… I’ll help however I can.</b> Her voice is laced with an eerie sincerity.